IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`
IMPORT `je21-art11-annulment`

-- je21-tests-art11-annulment: tests for Article 11.
-- The expected values were written by hand from Article 11 and the endnote (Part 2 in force on 28 September 2021) before the module was run.
-- A count of sittings is an input, so the tests give counts directly: 3 is in time, 4 is not.

§ `Article 11 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings (the first of each pair is the default)`

`L5 adopted` MEANS `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`
`L5 Law only` MEANS `made by the States means a Law only`
`L7 commencement` MEANS `the 3 sittings run from the commencement of Part 2, which is what paragraph (4) says`
`L7 laying` MEANS `paragraph (4) has no reference to apply to, so the 3 sittings run from the date of laying, as paragraph (1) says`
`L3 default` MEANS `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
`L3 refuse` MEANS `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`

§§ `11(3) The instruments Article 11 applies to`

#ASSERT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `an Order` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `an Order` TRUE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` TRUE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `Regulations` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `Triennial Regulations` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `a Law` FALSE `L5 adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `UK extended legislation` FALSE `L5 adopted`
-- On the other reading of "made by the States", Regulations and Acts are not made by the States and Article 11 reaches them.
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `Regulations` FALSE `L5 Law only`
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` FALSE `L5 Law only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `Regulations` TRUE `L5 Law only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` `a Law` FALSE `L5 Law only`

§§ `11(1) The duty to lay`

#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the duty to lay the instrument before the States has been met` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(1): the duty to lay the instrument before the States has been met` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(1): the duty to lay the instrument before the States has been met` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, so it does not say that the instrument must be laid"

§§ `11(1), 11(2)(a) Ceasing to have effect, for an instrument made after Part 2 came into force`

-- Made on 10 January 2022. The count is of sittings after the date it was laid, up to the resolution.
-- Both sides of the threshold of 3.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 0 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 1 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 2 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 3 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 4 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 10 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
-- The reading of L7 does not matter for an instrument made after Part 2 came into force.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 3 99 FALSE `L7 laying` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 4 0 FALSE `L7 laying` `L3 default`
-- No resolution to annul: nothing ceases.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) FALSE 1 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
-- A contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1).
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 1 0 TRUE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
-- Article 11 does not apply to the instrument.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` FALSE (YMD 2022 1 10) TRUE 1 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`

§§ `11(4) An instrument made before Part 2 came into force`

-- Made on 27 September 2021, laid on 1 December 2021, annulled at the second sitting after laying, which was the sixth sitting after 28 September 2021.
-- On the reading taken (L7) the 3 sittings run from 28 September 2021, so the resolution was out of time; on the other the 3 run from laying, and it was in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 2 6 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 2 6 FALSE `L7 laying` `L3 default`
-- The converse: the resolution was at the third sitting after 28 September 2021 but the tenth after laying.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 10 3 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 10 3 FALSE `L7 laying` `L3 default`
-- Both sides of 3 sittings after commencement.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE 9 3 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE 1 4 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
-- The edge day: an instrument made on 28 September 2021 itself.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE 3 99 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE 4 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE 3 3 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 refuse` BECAUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 2 of the Law came into force, so whether an instrument made that day was made before it cannot be answered"
-- And the day after.
#ASSERT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 29) TRUE 3 99 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 refuse`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 29) TRUE 4 0 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 refuse`
-- Not resolved, or displaced, or not applying: the same for an old instrument.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) FALSE 1 1 FALSE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 1 1 TRUE `L7 commencement` `L3 default`

§§ `11(2)(b) What annulment leaves alone`

#ASSERT `Article 11(2)(b): the annulment leaves alone what was done under the instrument and the maker's power to make further legislation` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(2)(b): the annulment leaves alone what was done under the instrument and the maker's power to make further legislation` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 11(2)(b) speaks of an annulment, and the instrument has not been annulled"
